---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="FAQ | plansplease"
  description="Answers about the plansplease CLI, cloud workspace, privacy, and alpha plans."
  activePath="faq"
>
  <section class="prose-page faq-page" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <h1 id="faq-title">Questions we expect to hear.</h1>
    <p>
      plansplease is early. These answers describe what works today, not a larger product we have
      not built yet.
    </p>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>What is plansplease?</summary>
        <p>
          It gives agent-made HTML a place to land. The CLI creates local previews. The cloud
          workspace keeps a private copy you can open later.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What can I upload?</summary>
        <p>
          The cloud alpha accepts one standalone HTML file at a time. The local CLI can also serve
          a page folder with an <code>index.html</code> entry point.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Are cloud pages public?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Cloud pages are tied to the signed-in account in the current alpha. Public sharing is
          not available yet.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Will there be a paid plan?</summary>
        <p>
          Maybe. The pricing page shows the current placeholder. We are considering storage,
          retention, and bundled uploads as paid features, but no payment plan exists yet.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I self-host it?</summary>
        <p>
          The source is public and self-hosting is part of the plan. The self-hosting path is not
          documented as a supported deployment yet.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .faq-page {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .faq-list {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--night-border);
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    transition: border-color 180ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item:hover {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 1.85rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    list-style: none;
    transition: color 180ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::after {
    content: "+";
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 1.8rem;
    height: 1.8rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(143, 227, 201, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(143, 227, 201, 0.25);
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--mint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    transition: all 180ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] summary::after {
    content: "\2212";
    background: rgba(200, 185, 247, 0.08);
    border-color: rgba(200, 185, 247, 0.25);
    color: var(--lavender);
  }

  .faq-item summary:hover,
  .faq-item summary:focus-visible {
    color: var(--mint);
  }

  .faq-item summary:hover::after {
    transform: scale(1.08);
  }

  .faq-item p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: -0.25rem 0 1.6rem;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .faq-item code {
    padding: 0.2rem 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 0.35rem;
    background: var(--night-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    color: var(--mint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
  }
</style>
